Author: Matthias Wenz <matthias@entire.io>
Date:   Thu Jul 9 15:21:40 2026 +0200

    trail update: support setting a trail's branch

    Add --set-branch to `entire trail update`, routing by trail state:
    - a trail that already has a branch is renamed via PATCH {branch}
    - a branchless trail gets a branch attached via POST /:number/branch
      ({action, branch_name}), linking an existing branch or creating it
      on the forge (--branch-action link|create, default link)

    Add --trail to select a trail by number/id/branch, the only way to
    reach a branchless trail. --branch stays a selector; --set-branch is
    the new value.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

